# NIL Workspace — Build Rules

Visual law lives in `.cursor/rules/00-nil-design-language.mdc`.
Tokens: `frontend/src/lib/styles/tokens.css`. Motion: `frontend/src/lib/styles/motion.css`.
IA: `FRAMEWORK.md`.

## Mandatory Checks Before Commit

```bash
cd frontend && npm run check && npm run build
```

Both MUST pass. No exceptions.

## Token Audit

```bash
# No inline hex except tokens.css / app.css / shaders
grep -r "#[0-9a-fA-F]\{3,8\}" frontend/src --include="*.svelte" --include="*.css" \
  | grep -v "app.css" | grep -v "tokens.css" | grep -v "motion.css"
```

## Color law

Chrome is greyscale (`--nil-*`). The only saturated color in Zone B/C is `--sev-*`.
`--brand-ember-*` exists solely for Zone A identity moments (cold open, lock screen,
session handoff, report cover) — see `00-nil-design-language.mdc` Law 1. If something
in the workstation is colored and it is not a severity, it is a bug.

## Motion

Use the ten primitives in `motion.css`. Do not write bespoke `@keyframes` in components.
SCANLINE is the only infinite animation. MAGNETIC max 3 per screen.

## GPU

See `40-nil-gpu.mdc`. Zone C (stream, findings, terminal) is transform/opacity only.

## Focus

`:focus-visible` uses `--nil-halo`, 2px, 2px offset. Never the browser default blue.

## Anti-slop

- No brand accent, no colored primary button, no gradient washes in Zone B/C (ember is Zone A only)
- No fake metrics or fabricated CVSS
- No emoji in product UI
- No chat bubbles — tool cards with meta headers
- No fake terminal chrome
- No CSS traffic lights (native Tauri overlay only)
- Elevation via `--lift-*` + hairline, not a grey drop-shadow under every card
- No per-section entrance stagger
